#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:56
#, no-c-format
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "Introduccion"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:58
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kolorlines; is a simple game. It is played by one player, so there is only "
"one winner :-) You play for fun and against the high score. It has been "
"inspired by well known game - <application>Color lines</application>, "
"written for DOS by Olga Demina, Igor Ivkin and Gennady Denisov back at 1992."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:64
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In 2000 &Roman.Merzlyakov; wrote a original version for &kde;. Roman "
"Roazilov added to it a cool <application>povray</application> generated "
"animation. Later in 2001 he ported it to &kde; 2 and made it conform to the "
"&kde; games standard."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:73
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using &kolorlines;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:75
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The main rules of game is as simple as possible: you move (using mouse) "
"marbles from cell to cell and build lines (horizontal, vertical or "
"diagonal). When a line contains 5 or more marbles - they are removed from "
"the field and your score grows. After each of your turns computer drops "
"three more marbles onto the field."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:81
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The increase in score depends on the amount of erased marbles and if "
"&kolorlines; shows the next balls. The increase will be smaller if you use "
"the information of what's next."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:86
#, no-c-format
msgid "More &kolorlines; features"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:88
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kolorlines; is wonderful in that it will allow you to kill 5 minutes while "
"you wait for that program to compile."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:89
#, no-c-format
msgid "Or, if nothing else, it will allow you to kill 5 minutes."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:96
#, no-c-format
msgid "Command Reference"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:99
#, no-c-format
msgid "The main &kolorlines; window"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:101
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There is a large area with marbles. At the right side a bar showing the next "
"three marbles to be dropped on the field. Underneath the field is the status "
"bar. Above it is the menu bar."
msgstr ""

